# LeakSanitizer suppressions for third-party allocations (Linux only).
#
# These leaks are NOT owned by mtg_cpp:
#   * SFML 2.6 keeps a process-wide FreeType library that is freed during
#     static destruction, i.e. AFTER LeakSanitizer's exit check runs. Any text
#     that is measured or drawn (sf::Text::getLocalBounds / draw) allocates
#     glyphs through FreeType and shows up here.
#   * The NVIDIA GL driver (libnvidia-glcore) leaks small one-time buffers when
#     a window is created.
# Both are one-time and bounded. Allocations with one of these frames in their
# stack are skipped; every other leak (including anything in our own code) is
# still reported and fails the build.
leak:libfreetype
leak:libnvidia-glcore
leak:libGLX_nvidia
leak:libfontconfig
